    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nThe distributive law states that multiplying a group of terms by a number is the same as multiplying each term separately by that same number and adding the products.\n\nContent:\nThe distributive law works no matter how many terms are inside the parentheses.\n\nContent:\nFor example, let's take a look at the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 4(a+2b+3)]\n\nContent:\nWe can expand this expression using the distributive law:\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/fcf29cd47a0f1a0aeed8f24d2601324a]\n\nContent:\nTherefore,\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 4(a + 2b + 3)|=; 4 \u22c5 a + 4 \u22c5 2b + 4 \u22c5 3|=; (4a) + (8b) + (12)|=; 4a + 8b + 12]\n\nContent:\nThe distributive law also applies when the multiplication occurs on the right of the parentheses. Let's see an example.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Distributing a Positive Number Over a Sum\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpand [MATH: (3p + 4q + 2)\\cdot 5]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nUsing the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number [MATH: 5\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: (3p + 4q + 2) \u22c5 5|=; 3p \u22c5 5 + 4q \u22c5 5 + 2 \u22c5 5|=; (15p) + (20q) + (10)|=; 15p + 20q + 10]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 4(3x + 2y + 1) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 12x \u2212 8y \u2212 4]\nb. [MATH: 7x + 6y + 4]\nc. [MATH: 12x + 8y + 4]\nd. [MATH: 12x \u2212 8y + 4]\ne. [MATH: 7x \u2212 6y \u2212 4]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (x + 5y + 2) \u22c5 7 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 7x + 12y + 5]\nb. [MATH: 7x + 12y \u2212 5]\nc. [MATH: 7x + 35y + 14]\nd. [MATH: 7x + 35y \u2212 14]\ne. [MATH: 7x \u2212 35y \u2212 14]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Tutorial: Dealing With Minus Signs Inside the Parentheses\n\nContent:\nThe distributive law also works when there is subtraction inside the parentheses.\n\nContent:\nFor example, we can expand the expression [MATH: 2(x+2y-3)] as follows:\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/db305655f322e8cff28208bb07e18bc7]\n\nContent:\nNotice that we keep plus signs ([MATH: +]) between the three terms. This helps us to avoid mistakes when multiplying with negative numbers.\n\nContent:\nNow, evaluating our expression, we have\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 2(x + 2y \u2212 3)|=; 2 \u22c5 x + 2 \u22c5 2y + 2 \u22c5 (\u2212 3)|=; (2x) + (4y) + (\u2212 6)|=; 2x + 4y \u2212 6]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Example: Distributing a Positive Number Over Sums and Differences\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpand [MATH: 4( 5+4a-2b)]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nUsing the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number [MATH: 4\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: 4(5 + 4a \u2212 2b)|=; 4 \u22c5 5 + 4 \u22c5 (4a) + 4 \u22c5 (\u2212 2b)|=; (20) + (16a) + (\u2212 8b)|=; 20 + 16a \u2212 8b|=; 16a \u2212 8b + 20]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 5(3x \u2212 2y + 2) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 15x \u2212 10y + 10]\nb. [MATH: 8x + 3y + 7]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 15x + 10y \u2212 10]\nd. [MATH: 15x + 10y \u2212 10]\ne. [MATH: 8x \u2212 3y \u2212 7]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (3 + 5x \u2212 2y) \u22c5 7 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 10x \u2212 12y \u2212 5]\nb. [MATH: 35x \u2212 14y + 21]\nc. [MATH: 35x + 14y + 12]\nd. [MATH: 35x \u2212 14y \u2212 12]\ne. [MATH: 10x \u2212 12y + 5]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Example: Distributing a Negative Number Over Sums and Differences\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpand [MATH: (3x - 5y + 1) \\cdot (-4).]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nUsing the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number [MATH: (-4)\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: (3x \u2212 5y + 1) \u22c5 (\u2212 4)|=; 3x \u22c5 (\u2212 4) + (\u2212 5y) \u22c5 (\u2212 4) + 1 \u22c5 (\u2212 4)|=; (\u2212 12x) + (20y) + (\u2212 4)|=; \u2212 12x + 20y \u2212 4]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u2212 2(3p + 7q \u2212 9) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 3p \u2212 7q + 9]\nb. [MATH: 6p + 14q + 18]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 6p \u2212 14q + 18]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 6p + 14q + 18]\ne. [MATH: 6p \u2212 14q \u2212 18]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (5x \u2212 2y + 4) \u22c5 (\u2212 5) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 25x + 10y + 20]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 7y + 1]\nc. [MATH: 25x + 10y \u2212 20]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 7y \u2212 1]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 25x + 10y \u2212 20]"
  }
